 ( { Better was } 23. Qf3 g6 24. Rfc1 Qe5 25. g3 h5 { aiming for ...h5-h4. } 26. h4 $1 { ⩲ Now Black's counterplay is reasonably under control, therefore White's position is slightly preferable. } ) 
Qxe4 { White gave up the pair of bishops to trade off Black's powerful knight, but the counterplay still persists. } 24. Rd2 ( { If } 24. Qe2 Nh4 25. f3 Qg6 { Black remains threatening, for example } 26. f4 Nf5 27. Qd3 Rxb6 $1 28. Nxb6 Nxe3 $1 { regaining the exchange: } 29. Qxg6 fxg6 30. Rc6 Nxf1 31. Rxd6 Ng3 { with level chances. } ) 
